<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Jind State</h1><p class="st-meta">1763 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Sangrur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the three Phulkian Sikh states of Punjab, linked by marriage to the Sikh Empire of Ranjit Singh.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gajpat-singh">Gajpat Singh</a>, a descendant of Phul, seized the area of Jind around 1763 after the fall of Mughal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirhind">Sirhind</a>, and received the title of Raja from the Mughal emperor in 1772. His daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-raj">Raj</a> Kaur married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maha-singh">Maha Singh of Sukerchakia</a> and was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Jind accepted British protection in 1809. Its capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangrur">Sangrur</a>, and Raja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarup-singh-of-jind">Sarup Singh</a>'s support for the British in 1857 earned him new lands. Jind had a 13-gun salute and a mixed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jats">Jat</a> population. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranbir-singh-of-jind">Ranbir Singh</a> ruled from 1887 until 1948.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Jind acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1947 and in 1948 was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/patiala-and-east-punjab-states-union">Patiala and East Punjab States Union</a>. Its lands are now divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/jind-state.jpg" alt="Jind State" width="320" height="519"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sketch_map_of_Jind_State.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-